+## Measured semantics
+
+- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error`, so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller ([validated by: bypasses onError when rejection is not an Error instance](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L311)).
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits, and is passed the accumulated usage across all provider rounds in that turn: each round's token counts are summed so a turn that ran tool calls reports the total cost rather than only the final leg ([validated by: sums token counts when both rounds report usage](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L43)).
+- A turn driven through two tool rounds sees usage summed across both rounds before the hook receives it: two provider calls with known token counts arrive as one total in `afterModelResponse` ([validated by: accumulates usage from multiple tool rounds into a single total](../../src/orchestration/reportUsageAcrossRounds.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).
+- A turn with no tool calls sees no change in what the hook receives: the single provider call's usage is passed through unchanged ([validated by: turn with no tool calls reports the same usage as before](../../src/orchestration/reportUsageAcrossRounds.acceptance.test.ts#L95)).
+- Rounds that report no usage are skipped in the accumulation; a turn where some rounds omit usage and others provide it still reports the sum of what was provided ([validated by: accumulates reported usage when some rounds report none](../../src/orchestration/reportUsageAcrossRounds.acceptance.test.ts#L107)).
+- When no round in a turn reports usage, the hook receives `undefined`, not `NaN` or zero ([validated by: turn with no usage reported on any round passes undefined to hook](../../src/orchestration/reportUsageAcrossRounds.acceptance.test.ts#L123)).
+- When both the accumulated total and the new round are `undefined`, `accumulateUsage` returns `undefined`, so a fully usage-free turn passes `undefined` to the hook rather than `0` or `NaN` ([validated by: returns undefined when both arguments are undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L29)).
+- When the accumulated total is `undefined` and the new round reports usage, `accumulateUsage` returns the new round's value as the starting total ([validated by: returns the defined value when the accumulator is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L33)).
+- When the accumulated total is defined and the new round reports no usage, `accumulateUsage` returns the accumulated total unchanged ([validated by: returns the accumulator when the new round reports no usage](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L38)).
